## 6. AGENT FLOW — BACKEND (services/agent_flow.py)

### POST /api/agent/start
body: { ticketId, paneId }
→ set ticket status → Investigating
→ broadcast WebSocket status change
→ return { flowId } to frontend
→ frontend polls GET /api/agent/flow/{flowId} for step updates

### Each Step — Async Sequential Execution
Steps run one after another. Each step:
1. Writes { stepNumber, name, status: "running", startedAt } to agent_steps table
2. Executes its logic
3. Writes { status: "done", output: {...}, duration } to agent_steps table
4. Returns output to trigger next step

Steps never run in parallel within one flow.
On exception: write { status: "error", error: message } to agent_steps table.

### GET /api/agent/flow/{flowId}
→ return all agent_steps for this flow with current status + output
Frontend polls this every 1s to update step cards UI

### Step 1: Incident Analyzer
- Input: ticket.title + ticket.description
- Call AI model via anthropic client (use model from .env or config)
- Prompt: extract { problemStatement, affectedSystem, severity, missingInfo[] }
- Save output to agent_steps
- After save: call rag_memory.search(problemStatement, topK=1, threshold=0.85)
- If hit: attach ragMemoryHit to flow, return flag to frontend

### Step 2: Problem Statement Finder
- Input: Step 1 output
- Call AI model
- Generate 2-3 line summary
- Save to agent_steps

### Step 3: Wiki & Documentation Search
- Call wiki_search.py (EXISTING — do not recreate)
- Try wiki search first
- On empty result OR any exception: catch it, log it, call doc_search()
- Show which source was used in output: "wiki" or "docs_fallback"
- Save top 3 results to agent_steps

### Step 4: Historical Memory Search (RAG)
- Call rag_memory.search(problemStatement, topK=3, threshold=0.65)
- Evaluate similarity tiers:
  > 0.85: highConfidence = true, offer fastTrack
  0.65-0.85: partialMatch = true, prePopulateQueries = cached queries
  < 0.65: noMatch = true
- Save results + tier to agent_steps

### Step 5: Query Generator
- Input: ticket + step3 results + step4 results
- Call AI model
- Generate: 2 SQL queries + 1 log query
- If partialMatch: include historical queries in prompt as starting point
- Save generated queries to agent_steps

### Step 6: SQL Executor
- Input: SQL queries from Step 5
- Call terminal_runner.py which returns mock structured data
- Mock data matches ticket:
  AWTI-I-5001: portfolio_allocations rows, rebalancing_jobs rows
  AWTI-I-5002: allocation_weights rows, portfolio_calc_runs rows
  AWTI-I-5003: fx_orders rows, account_setup_log rows
- Return: { command, rows[], executionTime, rowCount }
- Save to agent_steps

### Step 7: Log Query Executor
- Input: log query from Step 5
- Call terminal_runner.py for mock log lines
- Return: { command, logLines[], matchCount, executionTime }
- logLines each have: { timestamp, level, service, message, isMatch }
- Mock logs match ticket context
- Save to agent_steps

### Step 8: Final Answer Generator
- Input: fetch ALL agent_steps from DB for this flowId
- Call AI model with all outputs combined
- Generate:
  { rootCause, fixSteps[], confidenceScore }
- Save to agent_steps
- Set flow status: "awaiting_report"

